config INPUT_TMAG5273_NUB
	bool "TMAG5273 hall-effect trackpoint nub input driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_THUMBDECK_TMAG5273_NUB_ENABLED
	depends on I2C
	depends on INPUT
	help
	  ThinkPad-style rate-control pointing from a TI TMAG5273 I2C 3D hall
	  sensor reading a magnet embedded in a printed flexure spring (Ploopy
	  Bean architecture, adapted). Each poll converts X/Y field deflection
	  from the boot-calibrated zero into relative pointer motion through a
	  quadratic response curve: cursor VELOCITY follows deflection angle, so
	  the thumb never lifts. Emits INPUT_EV_REL X/Y for zmk,input-listener.
